nina: Filing PR to modernize our tool-calling examples to the new structured-output envelope. PR #4190. Focus: order-cancel, calendar-invite, and embeddings-re-rank examples. Need docs review and a quick link sweep.

rachel: Thanks. Can you spell out what the envelope looks like this time? We need a very tiny example for the migration guide.

nina: Proposal: top-level object with 'payload' and optional 'meta' and 'error' keys. Minimal shape: {payload: {...}}. We'll document exact JSON Schema in the guide.

sam: I'll own the calendar-invite conversion. Which example file path should I edit?

nina: docs/examples/flows/calendar-invite.md. Also update docs/intro/tool-calling.md to reference the new example.

luis: For SDK snippets: I'll add a Python and a JS safe parser. In Python I'll provide a simple recover_json helper using regex + json.loads.

rachel: Please include a short note about defensive parsing in the SDK docs: prefer schema validation after parsing. Also show how to return a helpful error to callers.

kevin: Suggest including a short test harness in docs-tests that loads the example outputs (snapshots) and asserts that our schema validator accepts them. I can add a quick AJV schema for the JS side.

nina: Great. Also note: embeddings example is referenced in the migration guide and the examples index. We need to update both and add a redirect from the old anchor. I'll open a small redirects PR after this one merges.

luis: Draft of JS safe parser I'll add to sdk/examples/parse-helpers.js: code snippet:
```js
// recoverJson attempts to extract the first {...} block and parse it
function recoverJson(text) {
  try {
    return JSON.parse(text);
  } catch (e) {
    const match = text.match(/\{(?:[^{}]|\n|\r)*\}/m);
    if (!match) return null;
    try { return JSON.parse(match[0]); } catch (_) { return null; }
  }
}
```

rachel: Nice. For the Python helper include a one-liner using regex search and json.loads. Keep examples minimal.

sam: License check: the embeddings snippet was adapted from an external gist. Legal wants attribution and to confirm MIT compatibility. I'll add an attribution comment and ping legal.

nina: Docs style: include before/after blocks for every snippet replacement in the PR description. docs-bot will flag missing diffs.

docs-bot: Reminder: include 'before' and 'after' fenced blocks for all migrated snippets. Missing ones will block merge.

kevin: Also add a tiny migration note in docs/migration/tool-calls.md that shows the envelope example and a one-line compatibility tip for servers expecting the old flat structure. I'll keep it <5 lines.

luis: I'll also add a note in the SDK README pointing to recoverJson and recommend validating with the provided schema helpers.

rachel: Can someone add a brief checklist in the PR description: files touched, redirects needed, tests added, legal attribution? That speeds reviews.

nina: Done in PR #4190 description. Checklist: (1) schema file added; (2) examples updated; (3) SDK helpers added; (4) tests added; (5) redirects to follow; (6) legal notified.

sam: I'll start review on the ecommerce order-cancel example once CI artifacts are up. Ping me when tests are added.

docs-bot: Preview deployed at https://deploy-preview-4190--docs.redwood.ai/tooling/structured-output-example (expires in 48h).

kevin: After merge, recommend a short announcement in #product-docs so PMs know examples changed. Small note, nothing big.

rachel: Agreed. Keep it factual: what changed and where to find migration blurb.

nina: Thanks all. I'll incorporate feedback and push updates in the next patch. Leaving this thread open for follow-ups. :sparkles:
